## 9. Detection Engineering

### YARA Detection
Use the generated YARA rule (rule.yar) with 24 Lync-specific and malicious indicator strings, or the following high-signature rule to detect tampered Lync binaries:
```yara
rule Tampered_Lync_Mespinoza {
    meta:
        description = "Detects tampered Lync/Skype for Business binaries with Mespinoza ransomware indicators"
        author = "llm_judge"
        date = "2026-08-08"
        hash = "ba3558c89e9ff2e308d3191c9b8717c6462a0763a46f25730f09ab56e55c65c7"
    strings:
        $lync_class = "Lync99WindowServerClass"
        $lync_mutex = "Lync99GlobalMutex"
        $lync_trace = "%LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\Office\16.0\Lync\Tracing"
        $dynamic_alloc = "VirtualAlloc"
        $cmd1 = "PrepareProcessCommand"
        $cmd2 = "HandleCommandResult"
        $cmd3 = "ProcessCommand"
    condition:
        uint16(0) == 0x5A4D and // MZ header
        uint32(0x3C) + 0x18 == 0x4550 and // PE header
        filesize < 1MB and
        any of ($lync_class, $lync_mutex, $lync_trace) and
        any of ($dynamic_alloc, $cmd1, $cmd2, $cmd3) and
        pe.checksum == 0 and // Invalid checksum
        not pe.authenticode_valid // Unsigned
}
```
*(source: yara_gen_v2, malcat anomalies, malcat strings)*

### Import-Based Detection
Flag PE files with Lync version info (`FileDescription=Skype for Business`) that import the following APIs: `IsDebuggerPresent`, `RegSetValueExW`, `VirtualProtect`, `LoadLibraryW`, `GetProcAddress`, `CreateMutexW`, `GetKeyState` (source: pe_imports, malcat anomalies).

### Anomaly-Based Detection
Flag GUI PE files with the following Malcat anomalies: `InvalidChecksum`, `UnsignedMicrosoft`, `HugeGapBetweenFunctions`, `DynamicString`, `ManyHighValueImmediates`, and a high-entropy (>100) overlay (source: malcat anomalies, malcat file_layout).

### capa-Based Detection
Use capa to detect capabilities associated with tampered legitimate binaries: registry modification, process termination, thread creation, file move/create, and dynamic library loading (source: capa rules).

